;; Regulatory source register for JPN-RECONSTRUCTION special-reconstruction-zone
;; (復興特区) procurement compliance.
;;
;; README.md says: "Every regulatory claim must cite the official Reconstruction
;; Agency source." docs/operator-guide.md requires "clear provenance (official
;; Reconstruction Agency source citation) for every requirement surfaced".
;; docs/business-model.md makes "a false or fabricated regulatory-requirement
;; claim" a HARD hold that "must be corrected against a cited Reconstruction
;; Agency source first".
;;
;; Until this file existed there was no such list. Three documents required a
;; citation against a set that did not exist, so no claim in this repository
;; could be traced to anything, and nothing could tell a real citation from an
;; invented one. This is that list.
;;
;; Shape is tx-data (a vector of entity maps), like every other EDN corpus in
;; this workspace, so it loads with
;;   (d/transact conn (edn/read-string (slurp "facts.edn")))
;; :source/id is the join key. A regulation not in this table has NO
;; spec-basis for this repository -- extend the table, never invent an id,
;; a law id, or a URL.
;;
;; VERIFIED BY `nbb scripts/verify-facts.cljs`, which re-fetches every entry
;; from the live authority. Each entry carries a :source/verify tag naming
;; WHICH check establishes it. The checks are NOT interchangeable, and the
;; reasons are the main thing this file has to teach.
;;
;; ── THE CITATION SURFACE THE AGENCY ITSELF LINKS TO CANNOT BE VERIFIED,
;;    AND IT IS ON THE SAME HOST AS THE ONE THAT CAN
;;
;; www.reconstruction.go.jp/topics/cat-114/sub-cat12-1/ (復興関係法令・基本方針)
;; cites statutes by linking to
;;   https://elaws.e-gov.go.jp/search/elawsSearch/elaws_search/lsg0500/detail?lawId=...
;;
;; That is a JavaScript single-page app. Measured 2026-08-27, following the
;; redirect the legacy elaws hostname issues:
;;
;;   .../document?lawid=423AC0000000122   (real)        200   800 B  e-Gov 法令検索
;;   .../document?lawid=999AC9999999999   (fabricated)  200   800 B  e-Gov 法令検索
;;
;; Same status, same byte count, same title, for a law that exists and one
;; that does not. The identifier never reaches the server in a way that
;; changes the response -- the shell is served first and the document is
;; fetched by script afterwards. A checker pointed here reports PASS for
;; every fabricated id anyone ever writes down.
;;
;; That is the whole failure this register exists to prevent, sitting on the
;; authority's own page.
;;
;; The sharp part is where it goes. elaws.e-gov.go.jp 301s to
;; laws.e-gov.go.jp -- so the surface that cannot discriminate and the
;; surface that can are THE SAME HOST, separated only by path:
;;
;;   laws.e-gov.go.jp/document?lawid=999AC9999999999      200  800 B   shell
;;   laws.e-gov.go.jp/api/2/law_data/999AC9999999999      404  code 404004
;;   laws.e-gov.go.jp/api/2/law_data/423AC0000000122      200  full text
;;
;; So "is this citation verifiable" is not a question about the hostname, and
;; an allowlist of trusted authorities would answer it wrong. It is a
;; question about the exact path, which is why :host/kind is declared per
;; entry-point here rather than per domain, and why the verifier proves the
;; indistinguishability each run instead of trusting this paragraph.
;;
;; The verifier REFUSES (exit 2) rather than checking a statute at the shell,
;; and resolves every statute at /api/2/law_data/ instead.
;;
;; ── A LAW ID IS NOT DERIVABLE FROM ERA, YEAR AND NUMBER
;;
;; 東日本大震災復興基本法 is 平成23年法律第76号. The id built from those three
;; facts the way every other Act in this file is built -- 423AC0000000076 --
;; is a 404. The real id is 423AC1000000076.
;;
;; The AC0/AC1 segment distinguishes a cabinet-submitted Act (閣法) from a
;; member-submitted one (議員立法), and nothing on the face of the citation
;; says which a given law is. 東日本大震災復興基本法 was member-submitted; the
;; 復興特別区域法 and 復興庁設置法 beside it were not.
;;
;; So an author who constructs ids instead of looking them up gets a
;; plausible-looking string that is wrong, and there is no reason a wrong id
;; must 404 rather than resolve to some unrelated statute. Every
;; :statute/law-id here was read back from the API, never assembled.
;;
;; ── A REPEALED REGULATION ANSWERS 200 WITH ITS FULL TEXT
;;
;; e-Gov keeps repealed law text served. Measured 2026-08-27:
;;
;;   423M60000100151  厚生労働省関係東日本大震災復興特別区域法施行規則
;;                    200, full text, repeal_status "Repeal"
;;
;; Status alone certifies it as a live obligation. For a register whose whole
;; job is telling a real requirement from an invented one, publishing a
;; repealed rule as current IS the fabricated regulatory claim that
;; docs/business-model.md calls a HARD hold. :statute/repealed? is checked on
;; every entry, and the repealed rule above is kept IN the register, marked,
;; as a live control that the check still discriminates.
;;
;; ── repeal_status IS THE STRING "None", NOT null
;;
;; For a law in force the API sends the four characters None inside quotes:
;;
;;   "repeal_status":"None"
;;
;; It is a truthy string in every language this workspace uses. A verifier
;; written the obvious way --
;;
;;   (if (:repeal_status rev) :repealed :in-force)
;;
;; marks EVERY law repealed, including the ones in force; written the other
;; obvious way, comparing to nil, it marks every law in force, including the
;; repealed one. Both fail silently in a direction that looks like a working
;; check. The verifier compares against the literal strings, and its
;; self-tests assert that a "None" is not read as a repeal.
;;
;; ── THE AGENCY'S OWN LINKS 301, SO THE URL YOU COPY IS NOT THE URL THAT
;;    ANSWERS
;;
;; Every deep link on this site redirects. Measured 2026-08-27:
;;
;;   /topics/000344.html            301 -> /topics/cat-11/cat-45/000344/
;;   /topics/main-cat12/sub-cat12-1/ 301 -> /topics/cat-114/sub-cat12-1/
;;   /topics/main-cat9/sub-cat9-1/   301 -> /topics/cat-93/sub-cat9-1/
;;
;; but /topics/main-cat12/ does NOT redirect, so this is per-page and cannot
;; be normalised by a rule. A verifier that does not follow redirects calls
;; three live pages dead; one that follows them silently loses the fact that
;; the recorded citation is a stale path, which is the thing an operator
;; needs to know before pasting it into a filing.
;;
;; So both are stored: :page/url is where the page actually is, :page/via is
;; the path the agency still publishes, and :page/redirects? asserts which.
;; A via-path that stops redirecting, or lands somewhere new, is a change in
;; the citation and is reported.
;;
;; ── THE PUBLISHED sitemap.xml NAMES A HOST THAT SERVES NOTHING
;;
;; https://www.reconstruction.go.jp/sitemap.xml is 1.1 MB and lists 7,594
;; URLs. Every one of them is on reconstruction.r-cms.jp -- the CMS vendor's
;; origin -- and not on the official host. Measured 2026-08-27:
;;
;;   https://reconstruction.r-cms.jp/                  403 Forbidden  118 B
;;   https://reconstruction.r-cms.jp/topics/000344.html 403 Forbidden 118 B
;;   https://www.reconstruction.go.jp/topics/000344.html 200         108 KB
;;
;; The site's only machine-readable index of itself is therefore unusable as
;; a citation source, and an ingest that harvested it would carry a vendor
;; hostname into a compliance record for every requirement it surfaced. It is
;; registered as :host/kind :non-authoritative-origin so that the next author
;; who finds the sitemap finds this note first, and the verifier asserts the
;; 403 still stands rather than leaving the claim as folklore.
;;
;; ── THE 404 PAGE CARRIES THE WHOLE SITE NAVIGATION
;;
;; www.reconstruction.go.jp answers a missing page honestly -- status 404,
;; title 「ページが存在しません。 | 復興庁」 -- but the body is 65 KB because
;; the site chrome is on it. So the obvious needles are on the missing page.
;; Measured 2026-08-27, against the 404 body:
;;
;;   復興特別区域     PRESENT   <- would pass on a deleted page
;;   調達情報         PRESENT   <- and this is the 調達情報 page's own <h1>
;;   東日本大震災復興特別区域法  absent   <- discriminates
;;
;; The procurement page cannot be checked by its own heading. Every
;; :page/must-contain in this file was tested against a live 404 body and
;; rejected if present, and the verifier re-runs that test each time so that
;; a needle which migrates into the site chrome is REFUSED rather than
;; quietly becoming decorative.

[;; ── HOSTS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 ;; Declared per host because they do not behave alike, and a verifier
 ;; written against one of them is wrong about the others.

 {:host/name "www.reconstruction.go.jp"
  :host/kind :page
  :host/charset "utf-8"
  :host/charset-in-header? true
  :host/missing-status 404
  :host/missing-title "ページが存在しません。 | 復興庁"
  :host/missing-probe "https://www.reconstruction.go.jp/topics/cat-114/"
  :host/note
  "Honest 404 (status AND distinctive title), UTF-8 declared in the header.
   Both are asserted at run time, because the needles in this file were
   chosen against this host's 404 body and stop meaning anything if it
   changes."
  :host/measured "2026-08-27"}

 {:host/name "laws.e-gov.go.jp"
  :host/kind :statute-api
  :host/api-base "https://laws.e-gov.go.jp/api/2/law_data/"
  :host/missing-status 404
  :host/live-repeal-token "None"
  :host/repeal-tokens ["Repeal" "LossOfEffectiveness"]
  :host/note
  "The only surface here that discriminates a real law id from a fabricated
   one. Returns 404 for an unknown id and 200 with full text for a known
   one, INCLUDING repealed ones -- see :statute/repealed?. Note this is the
   same domain that serves the indistinguishable SPA shell at /document;
   only /api/2/law_data/ answers the question."
  :host/measured "2026-08-27"}

 {:host/name "elaws.e-gov.go.jp"
  :host/kind :indistinguishable
  :host/probe-real "https://elaws.e-gov.go.jp/document?lawid=423AC0000000122"
  :host/probe-fake "https://elaws.e-gov.go.jp/document?lawid=999AC9999999999"
  :host/redirects-to "https://laws.e-gov.go.jp/document"
  :host/note
  "JavaScript SPA, and a legacy hostname: it 301s to laws.e-gov.go.jp, the
   SAME host that serves the discriminating API above. Same 800-byte shell,
   status 200, title 「e-Gov 法令検索」 for a real law id and a fabricated one.
   This is where the agency's own 復興関係法令 page sends a reader for every
   statute it cites. Registered as a distinct entry-point rather than folded
   into laws.e-gov.go.jp precisely because the domain does not determine the
   answer -- the path does. Page checks against it are REFUSED, never passed
   and never failed; a check that cannot fail is not evidence."
  :host/measured "2026-08-27"}

 {:host/name "reconstruction.r-cms.jp"
  :host/kind :non-authoritative-origin
  :host/expect-status 403
  :host/probe "https://reconstruction.r-cms.jp/topics/000344.html"
  :host/note
  "CMS vendor origin. Named by every one of the 7,594 <loc> entries in the
   agency's published sitemap.xml, and serves 403 Forbidden for all of them.
   Never cite this host. Registered so the trap is discoverable, and probed
   so the claim stays measured."
  :host/measured "2026-08-27"}

